{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>Now let Pharaoh look for a discerning and wise man.</b> He told him that he would need a discerning and wise man to be appointed over the whole land, and that he should further appoint officers under him to go throughout the land and gather all the food, for the governor cannot go throughout the whole land himself. And he told him that he must be discerning and wise: discerning — that he know how to manage the land of Egypt with bread according to the population, distributing from his own hand and giving them enough for their survival, and selling the surplus to the other lands to amass wealth and riches for Pharaoh; and wise — that he know how to preserve the grain so that it not rot, by mixing it with any substance that preserves it in its nature, such as the chalk that our Rabbis mentioned (Shabbat 31), and the live silver that kills the vermin, and similar things. And they said in Bereshit Rabbah (Genesis Rabbah 90:5): mix with it earth and chaff — things that preserve the grain. And Joseph said all this in order that they choose him, for the wise man's eyes are in his head:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:43:33.695438260Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}